  "region": "India",
  "level": "advanced",
  "given": {
    "O": "The centre of a decagon.",
    "A": "A point to the right of O. The decagon’s sides touch the circle through A."
  },
  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s SM6 drawing, whose pieces are drawn edge to edge. O is the centre of a regular decagon and OA its inradius. The decagons sit at the centre and the corners of a rectangle of half-sides 2φ and 2φ tan 54° (in OA, φ the golden ratio). Every line runs parallel to a side of the decagon, and, about some decagon’s centre, passes through it, along a side or at φ from it (drawing within 0.001 of OA). The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. Colours follow the shapes: Wichmann draws the kites dark green and the rest white, with the lines as red bands. No photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-27"
  },
  "credits": [
    {
      "source": "Tiling Search, data206/SM6: Friday Mosque, Fatehpur Sikri, India",
      "creator": "Brian Wichmann",
      "kind": "drawing",
      "url": "https://tilingsearch.mit.edu/HTML/data206/SM6.html",
      "note": "Read from his finished drawing, not construction instructions. His reference is E. W. Smith, The Moghul Architecture of Fathpur-Sikri, part 4 (1896), plate XXVII (Friday Mosque). He notes that Bourgoin’s plate 175 is the same pattern without some ornament."
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Draw a horizontal straight line through O and A. Draw a circle with centre O through A. It crosses the horizontal line again at F.",
      "create": {
        "c": {"circle": {"centre": "O", "through": "A"}},
        "h": {"line": {"through": ["O", "A"]}},
        "F": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 180.0}}}
      },
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Draw a vertical line through O. It crosses the circle at N.",
      "create": {
        "v": {"line": {"through": "O", "perpendicularTo": "h"}},
        "N": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "v"], "pick": {"angle": 90.0}}}
      },
      "highlight": ["c", "h"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Draw a circle with centre F through O. It crosses the first circle at Y1 and Y2. Draw a straight line through Y1 and Y2. It crosses the horizontal line at M, halfway from O to F.",
      "create": {
        "cW": {"circle": {"centre": "F", "through": "O"}},
        "Y1": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cW"], "pick": {"angle": 120.0}}},
        "Y2": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cW"], "pick": {"angle": 240.0}}},
        "m": {"line": {"through": ["Y1", "Y2"]}},
        "M": {"point": {"meet": ["m", "h"]}}
      },
      "highlight": ["F"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Draw a circle with centre M through N. It crosses the horizontal line at R.",
      "create": {
        "cM": {"circle": {"centre": "M", "through": "N"}},
        "R": {"point": {"meet": ["cM", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 0.0}}}
      },
      "highlight": ["M"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Draw a circle with centre A and opening from O to R. It crosses the circle at B and K. Draw circles of the same size round the circle, each centred where the last one crosses it. They mark C, D, E, G, H and J. The circle is now cut into ten.",
      "create": {
        "cF0": {"circle": {"centre": "A", "radiusFrom": ["O", "R"]}},
        "B": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF0"], "pick": {"angle": 36.0}}},
        "K": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF0"], "pick": {"angle": 324.0}}},
        "cF1": {"circle": {"centre": "B", "radiusFrom": ["O", "R"]}},
        "C": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF1"], "pick": {"angle": 72.0}}},
        "cF2": {"circle": {"centre": "C", "radiusFrom": ["O", "R"]}},
        "D": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF2"], "pick": {"angle": 108.0}}},
        "cF3": {"circle": {"centre": "D", "radiusFrom": ["O", "R"]}},
        "E": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF3"], "pick": {"angle": 144.0}}},
        "cF9": {"circle": {"centre": "K", "radiusFrom": ["O", "R"]}},
        "J": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF9"], "pick": {"angle": 288.0}}},
        "cF8": {"circle": {"centre": "J", "radiusFrom": ["O", "R"]}},
        "H": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF8"], "pick": {"angle": 252.0}}},
        "cF7": {"circle": {"centre": "H", "radiusFrom": ["O", "R"]}},
        "G": {"point": {"meet": ["c", "cF7"], "pick": {"angle": 216.0}}}
      },
      "highlight": ["R"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Draw a line through A at 90° to the horizontal line. Turn it round O by 36°, nine times. These ten lines touch the circle at A, B, C and on round. They make the decagon.",
      "create": {
        "t": {"line": {"through": "A", "perpendicularTo": "h"}},
        "tr": {"repeat": {"of": ["t"], "by": "rot10"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Turn the vertical line round O by 36°, four times. These four lines and the vertical line run through the corners of the decagon.",
      "create": {"vr": {"repeat": {"of": ["v"], "by": "rot10", "distinct": true}}},
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "The lines through A and D cross at P. The lines through C and K cross at Q. Draw a straight line through P and Q. Turn it round O by 36°, nine times. These ten lines make the outer ring.",
      "create": {
        "P": {"point": {"meet": ["t", "t@3"]}},
        "Q": {"point": {"meet": ["t@2", "t@9"]}},
        "f": {"line": {"through": ["P", "Q"]}},
        "fr": {"repeat": {"of": ["f"], "by": "rot10"}}
      },
      "highlight": ["A", "D", "C", "K"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "The line through C crosses the horizontal line at P1. Draw a vertical line through P1. It crosses the line through O at 54° at K1. Draw a horizontal line through K1. Turn both new lines round O by 180°. The four lines make the tile, with corners K1, K2, K3 and K4.",
      "create": {
        "P1": {"point": {"meet": ["h", "t@2"]}},
        "side": {"line": {"through": "P1", "parallelTo": "v"}},
        "K1": {"point": {"meet": ["side", "v@4"]}},
        "top": {"line": {"through": "K1", "parallelTo": "h"}},
        "frame": {"repeat": {"of": ["side", "top"], "by": "rot2"}},
        "K2": {"point": {"meet": ["side@1", "top"]}},
        "K3": {"point": {"meet": ["side@1", "top@1"]}},
        "K4": {"point": {"meet": ["side", "top@1"]}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler",
      "textWithoutHelpers": "The line through C crosses the horizontal line at P1. Draw a vertical line through P1. It crosses the line through O at 54° at K1. Turn the vertical line round O by 180°. K1, K2, K3 and K4 are the corners of the tile."
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "The right side of the tile crosses line PQ at P2, and the mirror image of line PQ at P3. Draw a line through P2 parallel to the line through E. Draw a line through P3 parallel to the line through B. Turn both new lines round O by 180°.",
      "create": {
        "P2": {"point": {"meet": ["side", "f"]}},
        "P3": {"point": {"meet": ["side", "f@8"]}},
        "m1": {"line": {"through": "P2", "parallelTo": "t@4"}},
        "m1x": {"line": {"through": "P3", "parallelTo": "t@1"}},
        "c1r": {"repeat": {"of": ["m1", "m1x"], "by": "rot2"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "The lines through A and E cross at P4. Draw a line through P4 parallel to the line through C. It crosses line PQ at P5. Draw a line through P5 parallel to the line through D. It crosses the line through A at P6. Draw a line through P6 parallel to the line through C. Reflect the new lines in the horizontal line through O. Turn all of them round O by 180°.",
      "create": {
        "P4": {"point": {"meet": ["t", "t@4"]}},
        "m2": {"line": {"through": "P4", "parallelTo": "t@2"}},
        "P5": {"point": {"meet": ["m2", "f"]}},
        "m3": {"line": {"through": "P5", "parallelTo": "t@3"}},
        "P6": {"point": {"meet": ["m3", "t"]}},
        "m4": {"line": {"through": "P6", "parallelTo": "t@2"}},
        "c2p": {"repeat": {"of": ["P4", "P5", "P6"], "by": "mirror:h"}},
        "m2b": {"line": {"through": "P4@1", "parallelTo": "t@3"}},
        "m3b": {"line": {"through": "P5@1", "parallelTo": "t@2"}},
        "m4b": {"line": {"through": "P6@1", "parallelTo": "t@3"}},
        "c2r": {"repeat": {"of": ["m2", "m3", "m4", "m2b", "m3b", "m4b"], "by": "rot2"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "The line through O at 54° crosses the line through P3 parallel to the line through B at P7. Draw a vertical line through P7. The right side of the tile crosses the line through K at P8. Draw a line through P8 parallel to the line through B. Reflect the new lines in the horizontal line through O. Turn all of them round O by 180°.",
      "create": {
        "P7": {"point": {"meet": ["v@4", "m1x"]}},
        "m5": {"line": {"through": "P7", "parallelTo": "v"}},
        "P8": {"point": {"meet": ["t@9", "side"]}},
        "m6": {"line": {"through": "P8", "parallelTo": "t@1"}},
        "c3p": {"repeat": {"of": ["P8"], "by": "mirror:h"}},
        "m6b": {"line": {"through": "P8@1", "parallelTo": "t@4"}},
        "c3r": {"repeat": {"of": ["m5", "m6", "m6b"], "by": "rot2"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "Join K1, K2, K3 and K4 to mark the tile that repeats.",
      "create": {"tile": {"polygon": ["K1", "K2", "K3", "K4"]}},
      "animate": "fade"
    }
  ],
